# Subagent + model routing (all projects)

Parent agents (Sol / Grok / Opus) must delegate easy work. Do not burn the parent on boilerplate, mechanical edits, command follow-through, or routine search.

Settings "Explore subagent model" affects Explore ONLY. For other Task subagents, parent MUST pass explicit model (or use an agent YAML that pins model).

## Default cheap model
| Role | Model | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Boilerplate / mechanical / follow a written plan | composer-2.5 | Default cheap coding worker |
| Explore / search | composer-2.5 (or Explore default) | Never Grok/Sol/Opus for Explore |
| Avoid for "cheap" | composer-2.5-fast, Grok Fast | Fast variants cost MORE |

## When to use which subagent
| Task | Subagent | Model |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Where is X / map repo | explore | composer-2.5 |
| Boilerplate, stubs, renames, glue, apply bounded plan | cheap-implementer else generalPurpose | composer-2.5 |
| Tests only | test-writer | composer-2.5 (unless hard design) |
| Docs after MATERIAL change only | docs-guardian | inherit/mid — cadence unchanged |
| Review finished diff | code-reviewer | mid/parent |
| Architecture, auth, Bifrost/MCP, security, migrations | PARENT / specialist | premium — do not downgrade |

Parent Task calls for easy work MUST set model: composer-2.5 (omission inherits Sol/Grok).

## Cloud agents
Use only when operator asks for isolated VM work without local secrets/Bifrost. Cloud = Max Mode + API pricing; Explore/Browser may auto-pick models; no local Bifrost. Not better for cheap boilerplate on this PC. Default local + composer-2.5.

## Git
After completed validated task slice: commit/push task-owned files only. Never git add -A on a dirty mega-tree.

## Anti-patterns
Parent writing boilerplate; Explore on Grok 4.6; Composer Fast to "save money"; cloud for Bifrost/live Windows ops; docs-guardian after every tiny edit.
